INT. REVOLVING RESTAURANT ATOP A SKYSCRAPER - NIGHT

The city turns slowly beyond a wall of glass. White tablecloths, low candles. A string quartet plays something sorrowful. Every table is full, except one.

At that table, three people sit in a tight triangle: AUGUSTINE KORMANN-DELACROIX (50s, charcoal suit, hands always moving), SALOME BRANDT-OYELARAN (40s, emerald dress, cool eyes), and WENDELIN ASHFORD-PETROV (30s, black turtleneck, a briefcase handcuffed to his wrist).

AUGUSTINE
Salome, you look radiant.

SALOME
I look hungry.

WENDELIN
The soup is good.

SALOME
Wendelin, it's soup.

WENDELIN
It's very good soup.

AUGUSTINE
(with a laugh)
Shall we order?

SALOME
We shall not.

She sets down her fork. He lays his napkin across his knee. The restaurant turns. A new skyline slides into view.

AUGUSTINE
You know why I asked you here.

SALOME
I have a theory.

WENDELIN
(clearing his throat)
She has several.

SALOME
I have one.

AUGUSTINE
Then say it.

SALOME
You want what's in the case.

Wendelin's hand tightens on the handle. Augustine lets the quartet play four more bars.

AUGUSTINE
I want you to open it.

SALOME
I don't have the key.

AUGUSTINE
You do.

SALOME
I don't.

WENDELIN
(quietly, to Augustine)
She doesn't.

AUGUSTINE
Then who does?

A beat. The restaurant turns again, and the three of them watch the city pass beneath them, glittering and indifferent. Salome lifts her water glass.

SALOME
Order the soup, Augustine.
